  "notes": "Found in a public repository and run by a computer-use agent (batch public-1). You pick or upload a chromatography-column or crystallizer model setup, and it writes out the governing equations in LaTeX, with assumptions, a symbol/unit table and literature references, which you can export as .tex, a CADET-Python template or a JSON config. Data used in the run: example. tree.json is the workflow the agent did and a second agent replayed; run.json says how.",
